From bb1cac586d5db387efdf34d5851114849c0eff86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:28:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] cpufreq: apple: T6050: Read the status register and
 switch from the scheduler

The T6050 profile verifies each request against the command register and
waits for it, so schedutil can no longer switch from the scheduler: every
change goes through the sugov worker thread, a wakeup and a context switch
per update on an otherwise idle system. Through the T8112 fallback the
J716s (MacBook Pro 16-inch, M5 Pro) switched from the scheduler.

Verify the scheduler's requests from a timer instead, as on T8140; the
waited-for paths (the static governors, suspend) are unchanged.

The status register has the T8112 layout: the current state is in bits
9:5 and the target in bits 4:0, read on M cluster 0 of the J716s, and
the T8112 fallback has reported all three clusters' frequency from it
on every J716s boot since. Report the current state from it,
so that cpuinfo_cur_freq shows the state the cluster runs at, which is
lower than the request when the cluster declines a boost state.

State 1 (300 MHz) is the lowest OPP of every cluster; refuse a level 0.

Assisted-by: LLM Claude
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c b/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
index fb87ae6ae137..0ec4bcedd9cb 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
@@ -341,12 +341,24 @@ static const struct apple_soc_cpufreq_info soc_t8132_info = {
 	.ps1_shift = APPLE_DVFS_CMD_PS1_SHIFT,
 };
 
-/* Command-state readback, not a measurement of the clock frequency. */
+/*
+ * T6050: requests are verified against the command register's readback, as on
+ * T8142. The status register has the T8112 layout (current state in bits 9:5,
+ * target in bits 4:0, read on the J716s), so ->get() reports the state the
+ * cluster runs at, which differs from the request when the cluster declines
+ * a boost state. State 1 is the lowest OPP. Requests from the scheduler are
+ * verified by a timer, as on T8140, so schedutil keeps switching from the
+ * scheduler as it did through the T8112 fallback.
+ */
 static const struct apple_soc_cpufreq_info soc_t6050_info = {
 	.verify_transition = true,
+	.lazy_verify = true,
 	.needs_firmware_thermal_control = true,
 	.transition_timeout_us = 2000,
+	.min_pstate = 1,
 	.max_pstate = 31,
+	.cur_pstate_mask = APPLE_DVFS_STATUS_CUR_PS_T8112,
+	.cur_pstate_shift = APPLE_DVFS_STATUS_CUR_PS_SHIFT_T8112,
 	.ps1_mask = APPLE_DVFS_CMD_PS1,
 	.ps1_shift = APPLE_DVFS_CMD_PS1_SHIFT,
 };
